Planex perception_phase2 — Phase 2 runtime validation
======================================================
Validates: px_perceptions_for_estimate + invoke_all + invoke_for_estimate

Setup:
  3 perceptions (a, b, c) depend on est1
  1 perception  (d)     depends on est2
  Total registered: 4

[test 1] px_perceptions_for_estimate(est1) returns 3 ... PASS (count=3)
[test 2] px_perceptions_for_estimate(est2) returns 1 ... PASS (count=1)
[test 3] px_perception_invoke_all() runs all 4 ... PASS (invoked=4, all counters == 1)
[test 4] px_perception_invoke_for_estimate(est1) runs 3 ... PASS (invoked=3, est2's perception stayed at 1)
[test 5] px_perception_invoke_for_estimate(est2) runs 1 ... PASS (invoked=1, est1's perceptions unchanged)
[test 6] invoke_for_estimate on unknown estimate runs 0 ... PASS (invoked=0)
[test 7] after free, invoke_all runs 3 (was 4) ... PASS (invoked=3, counter_a unchanged at 2)

Final call counts:
  perceive_a (freed mid-way): 2
  perceive_b:                  3
  perceive_c:                  3
  perceive_d:                  3

=== Phase 2 validation complete ===

What this proves:
  1. px_perceptions_for_estimate() returns correct matching set
  2. px_perception_invoke_all() runs every registered perception
  3. px_perception_invoke_for_estimate() runs only matching ones
  4. Isolation: invoking for est1 doesn't touch est2's perceptions
  5. Freeing a perception removes it from the invoke set

Phase 2 status: runtime can drive perceptions selectively.
Next step: integrate into px_app_run so perceptions drive rendering
(replacing the on_render callback). That requires API change to
px_app_desc — will be done in a separate commit.
